Z||000000||88formula||10-28-2001||09:39 PM||||Did anyone ever notice that the Stock tachometer is not very accurate? I noticed that there is a 200-rpm discrepancy from what the computer sees and what the tachometer reads using my scan tool. At a steady 80 mph the tachometer reads 3000 rpm and the scan tool reads 2800 rpm.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-28-2001||10:11 PM||||a 200 rpm difference isnt so bad really, most gauges arent 100% accurate anyways.  Also, it could just be your car, if you or someone else has messed with the needle or something.<P>93% accurate is pretty good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||10-28-2001||10:25 PM||||I would have been happy if mine was only off by that much- at about 5,000 mine was showing 6500. That is why I have "tach-Zilla" stuck on the dash. Besides, the programmable shift light and playback is pretty cool too.||||reg||1
